// Test: bugfixes/ssr_method_call_in_accum_intra_method_leak
// Semantic: SEM-loop-acc — accumulator loops that append the return
//   value of a call (free function or method) must reclaim not only the
//   per-iteration allocations declared OUTSIDE the call (already handled
//   by the outer `mem_scope_mark` wrap) but also the intra-call builder
//   growth stages of the callee.
//
// Regression: SSR-METHOD-CALL-IN-ACCUM-LEAKS-INTRA-METHOD-STAGES
//   (dashboard #0e49479a7e76) — refinement of SSR-STRING-CONCAT-LOOP-OOM-33151
//   (#8c113611781e). The 0.33.147 outer wrap fixed leaks from
//   `head = json.get(...)` shape statements sitting BETWEEN the
//   accumulator decl and the loop, but each `acc = acc + r.render()`
//   iteration still left the intra-method builder growth stages of
//   `render()` pinned on the main heap until end-of-loop. On the reported
//   SSR payload (12 iterations of ~1.7 KB html: blocks) peak main-heap
//   footprint pushed past the server's 128 MB WASM memory cap.
//
// Fix (this test): `rewrite_self_append_in_block` now wraps each
//   MethodCall / non-builtin Call fragment with a per-call
//   `scope_push` + `scope_pop_keeping` pair:
//
//     integer __mark = scope_push()
//     string  __tmp  = <call>()
//     __tmp = scope_pop_keeping(__mark, __tmp)     // pop BEFORE append
//     __sb_N = string_builder_append(__sb_N, __tmp)
//
//   The pop happens BEFORE the append so a builder-doubling reallocation
//   triggered by the append lands above the pop's final heap_ptr and
//   stays alive. Every intra-call temporary the callee malloc'd (its own
//   string_builder growth stages, per-call helper temps) is reclaimed;
//   only the final Clean string bytes survive to feed the outer builder.
//
// This test uses the exact minimal repro from the bug report — 12
//   iterations of a free-function call whose body walks a 5-stage
//   concat chain, forcing multiple internal string_builder doublings.
//   Pre-fix per-iter heap_ptr delta grew by 1416 → 2440 → 4504 bytes
//   at the doubling boundaries; post-fix it stabilizes at exactly the
//   final chunk length (~350 bytes). Run under wasmtime_runner it
//   completes cleanly in both cases (the 64MB runner cap is generous);
//   the actual 128MB failure only reproduces on the server host. This
//   test is a functional-correctness proof — the leak's memory-shape
//   effect is verified separately via __heap_ptr delta instrumentation.
//
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.153
//
// Expected output:
//   done

start:
	string acc = ""
	integer i = 0
	while i < 12
		acc = acc + buildChunk(i)
		i = i + 1
	print("done")

functions:
	string buildChunk(integer n)
		string s = "<div class=\"card\" data-slug=\"item-"
		s = s + n.toString()
		s = s + "\"><h3>Item "
		s = s + n.toString()
		s = s + "</h3><p>Long payload padding to force multiple doubling stages of the internal string_builder. Repeat repeat repeat repeat repeat repeat repeat repeat repeat repeat repeat repeat repeat repeat repeat.</p></div>\n"
		return s
